            "text": "An old pricing page can be evidence of a price that was once offered, but it usually cannot by itself establish the price currently in force.\n\nCurrent pricing is better shown by:\n- the seller’s live pricing page;\n- the operative contract, order form, or renewal notice;\n- dated invoices or quotes;\n- archived pages showing continuity; and\n- applicable terms governing price changes.\n\nAn old page may still control if the parties incorporated that version into a contract or if the contract fixes the price until properly changed. Otherwise, its age, effective dates, disclaimers, and any later updates determine how much weight it carries."
